            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A self-sanitizing positive airway pressure (PAP) system (500) is disclosed. The self-sanitizing PAP system (500) comprises: a positive airway pressure (PAP) device configured to generate a flow of pressurized air to be delivered through a PAP hose (110) and a PAP mask (112); a sanitizing system comprising a sanitizing gas generator (304) configured to generate a flow of sanitizing gas (302); and a PAP base unit housing (108), wherein one or more components of the PAP device and the sanitizing gas generator (304) are disposed at least partially within the PAP base unit housing (108). The PAP base unit housing (108) further includes a PAP base connector (116) configured to removably fluidly couple a first hose connector (111) of the PAP hose (110) to the PAP device to provide the flow of pressurized air to the PAP hose (110). The self-sanitizing PAP system (500) further comprises a sanitizing gas connector (502) configured to removably fluidly couple the first hose connector (111) of the PAP hose to the sanitizing system (500) to provide the flow of sanitizing gas (302) to the PAP hose (110).</p>
            </abstract>
